  (3) WHERE THE KNEE SITS relative to the gradients actually measured.
      The benchmark's sensed |g| is 0.58-0.97. A fix that saturates well
      below that range is sign-descent: correct, but magnitude-blind.
        mode   |d| @0.1     @0.3     @0.6     @1.0     @2.0    knee
  -----------------------------------------------------------------
        base     0.0803   0.2881   0.4174   0.1469   0.2612   0.170
     rescale     0.0071   0.0227   0.0551   0.1332   0.4379   1.280
       reset     0.0706   0.5456   0.5583   0.5417   0.4941   0.260

  'knee' is where the response reaches half its maximum. If it sits far
  below 0.58, the walk is a bounded SIGN step and the gradient's magnitude
  is discarded by construction - which would finally explain, exactly, the
  notes' recurring observation that direction survives and magnitude does
  not matter. Moving the knee into the operating range is then a separate,
  and cheaper, tuning question than either fix above.
